{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Thus he did.</b> This completes the acts of making (עשיות) in the account of the Tabernacle. From the verse (Exodus 25:8) ״ועשו לי מקדש״ until here you will find 248 acts of making in the work of the Tabernacle and its vessels, one by one when you reckon the count, and they correspond to the 248 positive commandments in the Torah — provided you remove the acts of making for the foreign elohim that were among them, for those acts are not included in the reckoning: from the verse (Exodus 32:1) ״קום עשה לנו״ until (Exodus 33:5) ״ואדעה מה אעשה״; and all the rest you will find to be 248 exactly. And since Israel said ״נעשה ונשמע״ and nullified the ״נעשה״ when they made the calf, therefore those acts of making in the account of the calf went out of the reckoning, because idolatry has no place in [the realm of] unity; and further, they correspond as well to the 248 limbs in man, for just as the Tabernacle is weighed against the world and encompasses the entire world, so too it encompasses all the Torah in the 248 positive commandments within it, and also man in the 248 limbs within him. And were it not for prolonging matters I would expand for you a full explanation of this matter, for Elohim made this opposite that."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:08:01.901676332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}